---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/legal-layout.astro";
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from "@workspace/types";
---

<LegalLayout
  canonicalPath="/terms"
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms governing access to and use of the Docita healthcare management platform"
  lastUpdated="November 26, 2025"
>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      By accessing or using Docita's healthcare management
      software and related services (the "Service"), you agree to be bound by
      these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you do not agree to these Terms, you may
      not use the Service.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      These Terms apply to all users of the Service, including healthcare
      providers, facility administrators, staff members, and any other authorized users.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">2. Description of Service</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Docita provides a cloud-based healthcare management platform that includes:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Patient record management</li>
      <li>Appointment scheduling</li>
      <li>Prescription management</li>
      <li>Billing and invoicing</li>
      <li>WhatsApp integration for patient communication</li>
      <li>Analytics and reporting</li>
      <li>Document management</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">3. Account Registration</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">3.1 Account Creation</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      To use the Service, you must create an account by providing accurate and
      complete information. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality
      of your account credentials.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">3.2 Account Requirements</h3>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>You must be at least 18 years old to create an account</li>
      <li>
        You must be a licensed healthcare provider or authorized representative of
        a healthcare facility.
      </li>
      <li>You must provide valid professional credentials when requested</li>
      <li>You are responsible for all activities that occur under your account</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">3.3 Account Security</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You must immediately notify us of any unauthorized use of your account or
      any other security breach. We are not liable for any loss arising from your
      failure to protect account credentials.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">4. Subscription and Payment</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">4.1 Subscription Plans</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Service is offered through subscription tiers with different features and
      pricing.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">4.2 Payment Terms</h3>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Subscription fees are billed in advance monthly or annually</li>
      <li>All fees are non-refundable except as expressly stated in these Terms</li>
      <li>We may change pricing with 30 days' notice</li>
      <li>Failure to pay may result in suspension or termination</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">4.3 Plan Activation</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Access to paid tiers starts after plan activation and applicable payment
      confirmation. Your workspace billing notices describe renewal dates,
      payment grace periods, and any action required to keep access active.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">5. Acceptable Use</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">5.1 Permitted Use</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You may use the Service only for lawful purposes related to facility management
      and healthcare delivery, in compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">5.2 Prohibited Activities</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">You agree not to:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose</li>
      <li>Violate applicable healthcare laws or regulations</li>
      <li>Upload malicious code or interfere with the Service</li>
      <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to systems or data</li>
      <li>Share account credentials with unauthorized persons</li>
      <li>Use the Service to store or transmit illegal content</li>
      <li>Reverse engineer or attempt to extract source code</li>
      <li>Resell or redistribute the Service without authorization</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">6. Data Ownership and Responsibilities</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">6.1 Your Data</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You retain ownership of all data you enter into the Service ("Your Data").
      You grant us a limited license to use Your Data solely to provide and improve
      the Service.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">6.2 Data Responsibility</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">You are solely responsible for:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>The accuracy and legality of Your Data</li>
      <li>Obtaining necessary patient consents for data collection and storage</li>
      <li>Complying with healthcare privacy laws and regulations</li>
      <li>Maintaining appropriate backups of critical data</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">6.3 Data Export</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You may export Your Data at any time using the export features available in
      the Service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">7. Intellectual Property</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">7.1 Our Rights</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Service, including software, designs, trademarks, and content (excluding
      Your Data), is owned by Docita and protected by intellectual property laws.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">7.2 License Grant</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Subject to these Terms, we grant you a limited, non-exclusive,
      non-transferable license to access and use the Service for internal business purposes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">8. Disclaimers</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">8.1 No Medical Advice</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Service is a practice management tool and does not provide medical advice,
      diagnosis, or treatment recommendations. All medical decisions remain the sole
      responsibility of the healthcare provider.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">8.2 Service Availability</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Service is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any
      kind. We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, Docita is not liable for indirect,
      incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including loss of
      profits, data, or goodwill.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Our total liability for any claim arising from these Terms or the Service is
      limited to the amount you paid us in the twelve (12) months preceding the claim.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">10. Indemnification</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Docita, its officers, directors,
      employees, and agents from claims, damages, losses, or expenses (including
      legal fees) arising from:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Your use of the Service</li>
      <li>Your violation of these Terms</li>
      <li>Your violation of applicable laws or regulations</li>
      <li>Claims related to Your Data or patient care</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">11. Termination</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">11.1 Termination by You</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You may terminate your account at any time by contacting support. Upon
      termination, you will lose access to the Service and Your Data.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">11.2 Termination by Us</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We may suspend or terminate your access to the Service immediately if you
      violate these Terms or for any other reason with reasonable notice.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">11.3 Effect of Termination</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Upon termination, your right to use the Service ceases immediately. We will
      retain Your Data for a reasonable period to allow export, after which it may be deleted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">12. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      These Terms are governed by the laws of India. Disputes arising from these
      Terms or the Service shall be resolved through binding arbitration in
      accordance with the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, with the seat
      of arbitration in Hyderabad, India.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">13. Changes to Terms</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We may modify these Terms at any time. Changes become effective when posted
      on this page. Continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance
      of updated Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">14. General Provisions</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li><strong>Entire Agreement:</strong> These Terms constitute the entire agreement between you and Docita</li>
      <li><strong>Severability:</strong> If a provision is invalid, remaining provisions remain in effect</li>
      <li><strong>Waiver:</strong> Failure to enforce a right is not a waiver of that right</li>
      <li><strong>Assignment:</strong> You may not assign rights under these Terms without our prior consent</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">15. Contact us</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 rounded-[var(--radius)] border bg-card p-4">
      <p class="font-medium text-foreground">Docita Legal Team</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Email:
        <a class="ml-1 text-primary hover:underline" href="mailto:admin@docita.work">admin@docita.work</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Support:
        <a class="ml-1 text-primary hover:underline" href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
